    {
      "eval_id": "bqml_009_mmm_channel_weight",
      "conversation": [
        {
          "invocation_id": "inv_bqml_009",
          "user_content": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "Can we assign a Weight of Influence score to each channel that accounts for the fact that Linear TV is not clickable?"
              }
            ],
            "role": "user"
          },
          "final_response": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "Media Mix Model (MMM) \u2014 Weight of Influence by channel (L12M, Bayesian Ridge with ad-stock transformation):\n[Channel table: channel, raw coefficient, ad-stock adjusted weight, % of total influence]\nLinear TV influence estimated via exposure proxy (GRPs) rather than clicks. Top influencers: [1. Channel A X% | 2. Channel B X% | 3. Channel C X%]. Note: non-clickable channels (TV, Audio) are modeled using lagged spend as proxy for exposure. Model R\u00b2: X.XX."
              }
            ],
            "role": "model"
          },
          "intermediate_data": {
            "tool_uses": [
              {
                "id": "tu_bqml009_a",
                "name": "run_bqml_mmm",
                "args": {
                  "model": "BAYESIAN_RIDGE",
                  "target": "transactions",
                  "channels": "all",
                  "non_clickable_channels": [
                    "linear_tv",
                    "audio"
                  ],
                  "ad_stock_transform": true,
                  "date_flag": "L12M"
                }
              }
            ],
            "intermediate_responses": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "eval_id": "bqml_010_video_adstock_decay",
      "conversation": [
        {
          "invocation_id": "inv_bqml_010",
          "user_content": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "What is the ad-stock or decay rate for Video ads? How many weeks does a Video impression continue to influence a transaction after the ad stops running?"
              }
            ],
            "role": "user"
          },
          "final_response": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "Video ad-stock decay analysis (L12M, geometric decay model):\nEstimated decay rate (\u03bb): X.XX\nHalf-life: ~X weeks (impression influence drops to 50% after X weeks)\nFull decay (below 5% influence): ~X weeks\nPractical implication: pausing Video spend does not immediately zero out its contribution \u2014 expect X weeks of residual transaction lift. Recommend maintaining some Video continuity rather than on/off flighting."
              }
            ],
            "role": "model"
          },
          "intermediate_data": {
            "tool_uses": [
              {
                "id": "tu_bqml010_a",
                "name": "run_bqml_adstock_decay",
                "args": {
                  "channel": "online_video",
                  "target": "transactions",
                  "decay_model": "geometric",
                  "date_flag": "L12M",
                  "max_lag_weeks": 12
                }
              }
            ],
            "intermediate_responses": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "eval_id": "bqml_011_black_swan_outlier_detection",
      "conversation": [
        {
          "invocation_id": "inv_bqml_011",
          "user_content": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "Were there any black swan events \u2014 months where Transactions moved independently of all channel spend? What caused them?"
              }
            ],
            "role": "user"
          },
          "final_response": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "Outlier detection (BQML anomaly model, L24M):\n[N] black swan months detected where transaction volume was >[X] standard deviations from model prediction given spend levels:\n\u2022 [Month A]: +X% above predicted \u2014 likely cause: [viral event / PR spike / competitor outage]\n\u2022 [Month B]: -X% below predicted \u2014 likely cause: [site outage / payment issue / macro event]\nResidual not explained by any channel spend. These months are flagged and excluded from saturation/MMM models by default."
              }
            ],
            "role": "model"
          },
          "intermediate_data": {
            "tool_uses": [
              {
                "id": "tu_bqml011_a",
                "name": "run_bqml_anomaly_detection",
                "args": {
                  "model": "ARIMA_PLUS",
                  "target_metric": "transactions",
                  "control_for": "all_channel_spend",
                  "date_flag": "L24M",
                  "z_score_threshold": 2.5,
                  "return_residuals": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "intermediate_responses": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "eval_id": "bqml_012_cluster_analysis_performance_months",
      "conversation": [
        {
          "invocation_id": "inv_bqml_012",
          "user_content": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "If we group months into High, Medium, and Low performance, what specific channel mix defines a High performance month?"
              }
            ],
            "role": "user"
          },
          "final_response": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "K-means cluster analysis (k=3, L24M, features: all channel spend shares + transactions):\nHigh performance cluster (X months):\n\u2022 Avg transactions: X | Avg total spend: $X\n\u2022 Defining channel mix: [Channel A] X% | [Channel B] X% | [Channel C] X%\n\u2022 Notably higher than average: [Channel A +X pp], [Channel B +X pp]\nMedium cluster (X months): [...]\nLow cluster (X months): [...]\nHigh-performance months are characterized by [description of distinguishing mix pattern]."
              }
            ],
            "role": "model"
          },
          "intermediate_data": {
            "tool_uses": [
              {
                "id": "tu_bqml012_a",
                "name": "run_bqml_clustering",
                "args": {
                  "model": "KMEANS",
                  "k": 3,
                  "features": "channel_spend_shares_plus_transactions",
                  "date_flag": "L24M",
                  "label_by": "transaction_volume"
                }
              }
            ],
            "intermediate_responses": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "eval_id": "bqml_013_display_elasticity",
      "conversation": [
        {
          "invocation_id": "inv_bqml_013",
          "user_content": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "If we cut the Display budget by 50% tomorrow, what is the predicted percentage drop in total Transactions?"
              }
            ],
            "role": "user"
          },
          "final_response": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "Display elasticity simulation (L12M regression model):\nCurrent Display spend: $X/month \u2192 baseline transactions: X\nSimulated at 50% Display spend ($X/month): predicted transactions: X\nPredicted drop: -X% (X transactions)\nElasticity coefficient: X.XX (X% spend change \u2192 X% transaction change)\nNote: this assumes other channels hold constant and no ad-stock tail from prior Display spend (conservative estimate). Full decay considered: -X% adjusted."
              }
            ],
            "role": "model"
          },
          "intermediate_data": {
            "tool_uses": [
              {
                "id": "tu_bqml013_a",
                "name": "run_bqml_elasticity_simulation",
                "args": {
                  "channel": "display",
                  "spend_change_pct": -50,
                  "target": "transactions",
                  "hold_other_channels_constant": true,
                  "include_adstock_tail": true,
                  "date_flag": "L12M"
                }
              }
            ],
            "intermediate_responses": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "eval_id": "bqml_014_ott_audience_uniqueness",
      "conversation": [
        {
          "invocation_id": "inv_bqml_014",
          "user_content": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "Is OTT providing a unique audience, or is it perfectly correlated with Social, suggesting we are reaching the same people twice?"
              }
            ],
            "role": "user"
          },
          "final_response": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "OTT vs Social audience overlap analysis (L12M):\nCorrelation of OTT spend with Social transactions: r=X.XX\nCorrelation of OTT spend with OTT-attributed transactions: r=X.XX\nIf OTT and Social are highly correlated (r>0.8) with no incremental transaction lift when both are active, they likely reach the same audience.\nConclusion: OTT and Social correlation = X.XX \u2014 [high overlap / distinct audiences]. Synergy test (both active vs single): [+/-]X% incremental lift. OTT [is / is not] reaching a meaningfully unique audience."
              }
            ],
            "role": "model"
          },
          "intermediate_data": {
            "tool_uses": [
              {
                "id": "tu_bqml014_a",
                "name": "compute_channel_correlation_matrix",
                "args": {
                  "channels": [
                    "ott",
                    "social"
                  ],
                  "metric": "spend",
                  "date_flag": "L12M"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "tu_bqml014_b",
                "name": "compute_channel_synergy",
                "args": {
                  "channel_pair": [
                    "ott",
                    "social"
                  ],
                  "target": "transactions",
                  "date_flag": "L12M",
                  "active_threshold_spend": 1000
                }
              }
            ],
            "intermediate_responses": []
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}